Title: In HTML form with email field, a browser message &quot;View Saved Logins&quot; covers up the &quot;Please enter an email address&quot; message.
Body: <p>I have a simple HTML form, something like:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;form action = &quot;register.php&quot; method = &quot;post&quot; autocomplete = &quot;off&quot;&gt; 
    &lt;input type = &quot;email&quot; name = &quot;email&quot; placeholder = &quot;Email&quot; id = &quot;email&quot; required&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;submit&quot; value=&quot;Register&quot;&gt;    
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>By setting <code>type = &quot;email&quot;</code>, some helpful validation features are activated. For example if I enter an &quot;email&quot; that does not have the @ symbol and try to submit the form, a message &quot;Please enter an email address&quot; will appear. Unfortunately, in my browser (Firefox), this helpful message is covered up by a &quot;View Saved Logins&quot; message. Is there any way to prevent this, for example by changing the position of one of the messages?</p>

answer:
To prevent the "View Saved Logins" message from covering up the "Please enter an email address" message in Firefox, you can adjust the CSS properties of both messages to ensure they do not overlap. Here's how you can modify your HTML:

```html
<style>
  #email {
    margin-bottom: 10px; /* Add some space below the email input */
  }
  .login-message {
    display: none; /* Hide the login message initially */
  }
</style>

<form action="register.php" method="post" autocomplete="off">
  <label for="email">Email</label>
  <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Email" id="email" required>
  <input type="submit" value="Register">

  <!-- Additional fields or elements -->
</form>

<script>
  // JavaScript to show/hide the login message
  document.getElementById('email').addEventListener('blur', function() {
    var loginMessage = document.querySelector('.login-message');
    if (!this.value.includes('@')) {
      loginMessage.style.display = 'block';
    } else {
      loginMessage.style.display = 'none';
    }
  });
</script>
```

In this solution:
1. We added a `margin-bottom` property to the email input to give it some space below it, which helps in preventing the "View Saved Logins" message from overlapping with the email input.
2. We added a new class `.login-message` to style the message that should be hidden initially.
3. We added a JavaScript event listener to the email input field that checks if the email input has an '@' symbol. If not, it shows the "Login Message".
4. You may need to adjust the styles further depending on your specific design requirements.

This approach ensures that the "Please enter an email address" message is always visible and does not get covered up by other elements in your form.

