    }
</code></pre>
<p>due to this the calendar icon is not visible, how should i style the icon. I want the icon to be yellow color to match the theme</p>
<p>I tried using :before pseudo element , but it didn't do anything
I want the code to support every browser</p>
<pre><code>input[type=date]:before {
  content: '\1F4C5'; 
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 16px;
  position: absolute;
  right: 10px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  cursor: pointer;
}
</code></pre>

answer:
To style the Calendar icon in a date input so that it displays as a yellow color, you can use the `::after` pseudo-element instead of `::before`. The `::after` pseudo-element allows for more complex styling options compared to `::before`.

Here's the updated CSS:

```css
.input::after {
  content: '\1F4C5';
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 16px;
  position: absolute;
  right: 10px;
  top: 50%;
  transform: translateY(-50%);
  cursor: pointer;
  color: yellow; /* Change the color to yellow */
}
```

Explanation:
- `.input::after`: This selects the `::after` pseudo-element of an element with the class `input`.
- `content: '\1F4C5';`: This sets the content of the pseudo-element to the Unicode character for a calendar icon.
- `font-family: Arial, sans-serif;`: This specifies the font family used for the icon.
- `font-size: 16px;`: This sets the size of the icon.
- `position: absolute;`: This positions the pseudo-element relative to its parent.
- `right: 10px;`: This moves the pseudo-element to the right by 10 pixels.
- `top: 50%;`: This centers the pseudo-element vertically.
- `transform: translateY(-50%);`: This ensures that the pseudo-element's y-coordinate is centered.
- `cursor: pointer;`: This changes the cursor to a pointer when hovering over the pseudo-element.
- `color: yellow;`: This changes the color of the calendar icon to yellow.

This approach ensures that the calendar icon will appear correctly in all modern browsers, including those that may not support the `::before` pseudo-element.

