Title: How to resolve No value accessor for form control name in Angular?.
Body: <p>I am trying to achieve the following where I can wrap <code>&lt;app-test-field&gt;</code> components inside the <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> tag where I can dynamically bind in <code>formControlName</code> and <code>formGroup</code> to TestField input as follows using Angular with StorybookJS.</p>
<p>However, I am encountering the following errors:</p>
<ul>
<li>core.mjs:11483 ERROR Error: NG01203: No value accessor for form control name: 'name'.</li>
<li>core.mjs:11483 ERROR Error: NG01050: formControlName must be used with a parent formGroup directive.  You'll want to add a formGroup directive and pass it an existing FormGroup instance (you can create one in your class).</li>
</ul>
<p>In <strong>TestField.stories.js</strong></p>
<p>Here is the template for my Angular component in StorybookJS.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;form [formGroup]=&quot;sampleForm&quot;&gt;
  &lt;!-- name input --&gt;
  &lt;app-test-field [label]=&quot;label&quot; [formControlName]=&quot;formControlName&quot;&gt;&lt;/app-test-field&gt;  
  &lt;!-- email input... --&gt;  
  &lt;!-- more inputs... --&gt; 
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>In <strong>test-field.component.html</strong></p>
<pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;form-group&quot;&gt;
  &lt;label for=&quot;{{ formControlName }}&quot;&gt;{{ label }}&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input
    type=&quot;text&quot;
    class=&quot;form-control&quot;
    [formControlName]=&quot;formControlName&quot;
    [id]=&quot;formControlName&quot;
  /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>In <strong>test-field.component.ts</strong></p>
<pre><code>import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-test-field',
  templateUrl: './test-field.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./test-field.component.css'],
})
export class TestFieldComponent {
  @Input() label: string = '';
  @Input() formControlName: string = '';
}
</code></pre>
<p>I researched most examples online where the input itself is wrapped around with the <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> tag in the component itself as below:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;form [formGroup]=&quot;registerForm&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;form-group&quot;&gt;
    &lt;label&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; class=&quot;form-control&quot; [ngClass]=&quot;inputDanger&quot; formControlName=&quot;name&quot;&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;br/&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>But I want to remove <code>form</code> tag such that the end goal would be the following where input is a component by itself wrapped inside a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> tag as follows:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;form [formGroup]=&quot;sampleForm&quot;&gt;
  &lt;!-- name input --&gt;
  &lt;app-test-field [label]=&quot;label&quot; [formControlName]=&quot;formControlName&quot;&gt;&lt;/app-test-field&gt;  
  &lt;!-- email input... --&gt;  
  &lt;!-- more inputs... --&gt; 
&lt;/form&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Can someone help me with this? Is anything missing?</p>

answer:
To resolve the issue of "No value accessor for form control name" and "formControlName must be used with a parent formGroup directive," you need to ensure that the `formControlName` is correctly associated with the `formGroup` in your Angular component. Here's how you can modify your code:

1. **Ensure the `formGroup` is defined in the parent component or another relevant component**:
   ```typescript
   import { Component } from '@angular/core';
   import { FormBuilder, FormGroup } from '@angular/forms';

   @Component({
     selector: 'app-root',
     templateUrl: './app.component.html',
     styleUrls: ['./app.component.css']
   })
   export class AppComponent {
     sampleForm: FormGroup;

     constructor(private fb: FormBuilder) {
       this.sampleForm = this.fb.group({
         name: '',
         email: ''
       });
     }
   }
   ```

2. **Pass the `formGroup` to the child component**:
   ```html
   <!-- app-root.component.html -->
   <form [formGroup]="sampleForm">
     <app-test-field [label]="label" [formControlName]="nameControlName"></app-test-field>
     <app-test-field [label]="emailLabel" [formControlName]="emailControlName"></app-test-field>
   </form>
   ```

3. **Update the child component to use the passed `formGroup`**:
   ```typescript
   // test-field.component.ts
   import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';
   import { FormBuilder, FormGroup } from '@angular/forms';

   @Component({
     selector: 'app-test-field',
     templateUrl: './test-field.component.html',
     styleUrls: ['./test-field.component.css']
   })
   export class TestFieldComponent {
     @Input() label: string = '';
     @Input() formControlName: string = '';

     constructor(private fb: FormBuilder) {}

     ngOnInit() {
       if (!this.formControlName) {
         this.formControlName = `${this.label.toLowerCase().replace(' ', '_')}`;
       }
     }

     getFormControl(): FormControl {
       return this.sampleForm.get(this.formControlName);
     }
   }
   ```

4. **Update the child component's HTML to use the `getFormControl()` method**:
   ```html
   <!-- test-field.component.html -->
   <div class="form-group">
     <label for="{{ formControlName }}">{{ label }}</label>
     <input
       type="text"
       class="form-control"
       [formControl]="getFormControl()"
       [id]="formControlName"
     />
     <br/>
   </div>
   ```

By following these steps, you should be able to resolve the "No value accessor for form control name" error and successfully bind the `formControlName` to the `app-test-field` component within the `form` tag.

