In this solution, we create a custom class `MyArray` that extends the built-in `Array` class. We then define a static method `toSorted` inside this class that takes an array and an optional comparison function, which allows us to sort the array according to our needs.

By using `MyArray.toSorted(x)` instead of directly calling `x.toSorted()`, TypeScript will recognize that `MyArray` has a `toSorted` method available. This approach ensures that you can use the `toSorted` method without encountering the type error you encountered.

